\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of RUSH-EEG2Text. (a)\nobreakspace  {}During natural reading, 105-channel EEG is artifact-masked, robustly calibrated per subject, and pooled into 12 bilateral cortical ROIs. Fixated words, ordered by the chronological scanpath (dashed arc: regression), form 488-d node vectors $\mathbf  {v}_t$, while sentence-level wPLI, iCoh, Log-Euclidean SPD, and left--right asymmetry features form a 2064-d connectome descriptor $\mathbf  {c}_{\mathrm  {sent}}$. (b)\nobreakspace  {}Stage\nobreakspace  {}1 uses a continuous $[0,1]$ scanpath-progress Fourier encoding (open circles: holistic sentence token) instead of integer positions, a 3D-grounded node Transformer, and a Perceiver resampler with $K=24$ latent queries $\mathbf  {H}_q$; a zero-initialized late connectome bottleneck fusion adapter injects $\mathbf  {c}_{\mathrm  {sent}}$ before a coarse-to-fine EMA-RVQ produces discrete brain tokens $\mathbf  {Z}_q$. (c)\nobreakspace  {}Stage\nobreakspace  {}2 projects $\mathbf  {Z}_q$ into a neural prefix for a LoRA-adapted Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, which is trained with scheduled target-word dropout and decoded by teacher-forcing-free beam search. Dashed gray boxes are training-only; the red box is the test-time Gaussian-noise sanity audit. Electrode layout, scanpath, and heat maps are schematic; the example sentence is taken from Table\nobreakspace  {}V.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{4}{Overview of RUSH-EEG2Text. (a)~During natural reading, 105-channel EEG is artifact-masked, robustly calibrated per subject, and pooled into 12 bilateral cortical ROIs. Fixated words, ordered by the chronological scanpath (dashed arc: regression), form 488-d node vectors $\mathbf {v}_t$, while sentence-level wPLI, iCoh, Log-Euclidean SPD, and left--right asymmetry features form a 2064-d connectome descriptor $\mathbf {c}_{\mathrm {sent}}$. (b)~Stage~1 uses a continuous $[0,1]$ scanpath-progress Fourier encoding (open circles: holistic sentence token) instead of integer positions, a 3D-grounded node Transformer, and a Perceiver resampler with $K=24$ latent queries $\mathbf {H}_q$; a zero-initialized late connectome bottleneck fusion adapter injects $\mathbf {c}_{\mathrm {sent}}$ before a coarse-to-fine EMA-RVQ produces discrete brain tokens $\mathbf {Z}_q$. (c)~Stage~2 projects $\mathbf {Z}_q$ into a neural prefix for a LoRA-adapted Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, which is trained with scheduled target-word dropout and decoded by teacher-forcing-free beam search. Dashed gray boxes are training-only; the red box is the test-time Gaussian-noise sanity audit. Electrode layout, scanpath, and heat maps are schematic; the example sentence is taken from Table~V}{figure.1}{}}
